  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/pseudo-melito-clavis#PsMelito.Clavis.19",
    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-melito-clavis",
    "canonical_ref": "PsMelito.Clavis.19",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "The womb of the Lord—the hidden recess of Deity out of which He brought forth His Son. In the Psalm: “Out of the womb, before Lucifer, have I borne Thee.”",
    "chunk_index": 19,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      600,
      1000
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/pseudo-melito-clavis#PsMelito.Clavis.20",
    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-melito-clavis",
    "canonical_ref": "PsMelito.Clavis.20",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "The feet of the Lord—His immoveableness and eternity. In the Psalm: “And thick darkness was under His feet.”",
    "chunk_index": 20,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      600,
      1000
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/pseudo-melito-clavis#PsMelito.Clavis.21",
    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-melito-clavis",
    "canonical_ref": "PsMelito.Clavis.21",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "The throne of the Lord—angels, or saints, or simply sovereign dominion. In the Psalm: “Thy throne, O God, is for ever and ever.”",
    "chunk_index": 21,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      600,
      1000
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/pseudo-melito-clavis#PsMelito.Clavis.22",
    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-melito-clavis",
    "canonical_ref": "PsMelito.Clavis.22",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Seat—the same as above, angels or saints, because the Lord sits upon these. In the Psalm: “The Lord sat upon His holy seat.”",
    "chunk_index": 22,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      600,
      1000
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/pseudo-melito-clavis#PsMelito.Clavis.23",
    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-melito-clavis",
    "canonical_ref": "PsMelito.Clavis.23",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "The descent of the Lord—His visitation of men. As in Micah: “Behold, the Lord shall come forth from His place; He shall come down trampling under foot the ends of the earth.” Likewise in a bad sense. In Genesis: “The Lord came down to see the tower.”",
    "chunk_index": 23,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      600,
      1000
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/pseudo-melito-clavis#PsMelito.Clavis.24",
    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-melito-clavis",
    "canonical_ref": "PsMelito.Clavis.24",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "The ascent of the Lord—the raising up of man, who is taken from earth to heaven. In the Psalm: “Who ascendeth above the heaven of heavens to the east.”",
    "chunk_index": 24,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      600,
      1000
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/pseudo-melito-clavis#PsMelito.Clavis.25",
    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-melito-clavis",
    "canonical_ref": "PsMelito.Clavis.25",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "The standing of the Lord—the patience of the Deity, by which He bears with sinners that they may come to repentance. As in Habakkuk: “He stood and measured the earth; and in the Gospel: “Jesus stood, and bade him be called,” that is, the blind man.",
    "chunk_index": 25,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      600,
      1000
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/pseudo-melito-clavis#PsMelito.Clavis.26",
    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-melito-clavis",
    "canonical_ref": "PsMelito.Clavis.26",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "The transition of the Lord—His assumption of our flesh, through which by His birth, His death, His resurrection, His ascent into heaven, He made transitions, so to say. In the Song of Songs: “Behold, He cometh, leaping upon the mountains, bounding over the hills.”",
    "chunk_index": 26,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      600,
      1000
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/pseudo-melito-clavis#PsMelito.Clavis.27",
    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-melito-clavis",
    "canonical_ref": "PsMelito.Clavis.27",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "The going of the Lord—His coming or visitation. In the Psalm.",
    "chunk_index": 27,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      600,
      1000
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/pseudo-melito-clavis#PsMelito.Clavis.28",
    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-melito-clavis",
    "canonical_ref": "PsMelito.Clavis.28",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "The way of the Lord—the operation of the Deity. As in Job, in speaking of the devil: “He is the beginning of the ways of the Lord.”",
    "chunk_index": 28,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      600,
      1000
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/pseudo-melito-clavis#PsMelito.Clavis.29",
    "work_id": "anf-works/pseudo-melito-clavis",
    "canonical_ref": "PsMelito.Clavis.29",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Again: The ways of the Lord—His precepts. In Hosea: “For the ways of the Lord are straight, and the just shall walk in them.”",
    "chunk_index": 29,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
